@flexiarg cascade-fold/search-when-path-is-unclear
@title Search the Fold (when no single construction is evident)
@keywords cascade, fold, wiring, search, tension, pivot, triage, dissolve, candidate, backtrack, explore, obligation, construction, compose, select
@audience fold engineers, proof architects, research agents
@tone strategic
@factor Keen investigation (dhammavicaya)
@style construction-strategy

! conclusion:
  When no single construction is evident, treat folding the cascade as a tension-
  resolving SEARCH: explore candidate constructions, triage and pivot, name the
  governing tension, dissolve it by re-choosing the construction, track to done;
  surface undissolved tensions as policy-holes.

  + context: You hold a cascade and a sorry stated as IF/HOWEVER tensions, and NO
    single construction is evident — several candidate constructions exist, none
    obviously right, and you cannot select or order their contributions by inspection.

  + IF: You hold a cascade and a sorry stated as IF/HOWEVER tensions, and no single
    construction is evident — several candidate constructions exist, none obviously
    right, and you cannot select or order their contributions by inspection.

  + HOWEVER: Committing to one path (a fixed pipeline) hard-codes a guess; the
    governing tension (expressiveness versus parsimony) is not resolved by any one
    fixed decomposition. You cannot compile an answer you cannot yet see.
    + FAILURE-MODES:
        - All candidate constructions are blocked -> output "no known construction"
          (the under-determination is a structural result, not a failure).
        - A seemingly-good candidate hides a node as hard as the original sorry.

  + THEN:
      1. Restate the sorry as IF/HOWEVER tensions (its failure-modes).
      2. Explore candidate constructions; mark each node solid / open / blocked.
      3. Triage immediately: kill blocked, prefer parallel; record abandoned approaches and why.
      4. Name the governing tension precisely: both obligations, the shared parameter, the conflict.
      5. Dissolve it by re-choosing the construction so both obligations agree.
      6. Track next-steps to done; surface undissolved tensions as explicit policy-holes.

  + BECAUSE: The governing tension (expressiveness versus parsimony) is not resolved
    by any one fixed decomposition; you cannot compile an answer you cannot yet see, so
    the fold must be a search that explores, triages, and dissolves the tension by
    re-choosing the construction.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
      - Restate the sorry as IF/HOWEVER tensions and explore candidate constructions, marking each node solid / open / blocked.
      - Triage immediately (kill blocked, prefer parallel, record abandoned approaches), then name the governing tension precisely and dissolve it by re-choice.
      - Track next-steps to done; surface undissolved tensions as explicit policy-holes.

  + QUALITY-CRITERIA:
      Well-applied: candidates sketched with explicit node status; the tension is named and dissolved by re-choice; pivots recorded.
      Badly-applied: collapsed to one pipeline prematurely; the governing tension left implicit.
